    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As milder spring weather set in, the defenders securing the nation's frontier confronted a surge in border confrontations, apprehending 8,268 people in March alone. This decisive action maintained the enforcement policy outcome: crossings remain near multi-decade lows. Yet the mission faces a political deadlock, with legislators deadlocked over funding, leaving the federal law enforcement agency without the resources it needs.",
